{"metadata":{"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Swidux","externalID":"Swidux","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"Swidux-logo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}]},{"anchor":"Companion-Packages","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Companion Packages"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a preview mock, and publishes its own DocC reference:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","isActive":true},{"text":" — RevenueCat adapter for the paywall plugin (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" sheet). See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","isActive":true},{"text":" — Mixpanel adapter for the analytics plugin (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"text":"). See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]